# Q4 planning

Monday, September 28, 2026 at 10:01 · 1 h 22 min

## Attendees

- Aisha Rahman
- Shreyas
- Maya Chen
- Diego Alvarez
- Priya Nair
- Tom Becker
- Noor Haddad
- Lena Okafor

## Notes

#### Decisions

- Calendar Sync v1 is bug-fix only for Q4; all new sync work goes into Calendar Sync v2.
- The Q4 priorities are, in order: Calendar Sync v2, SOC 2 Type II (observation window starting 1 November), offline mode for the technician mobile app, and the new-customer onboarding revamp.
- Route optimisation is cut from Q4, with no work on it at all, not even a spike.
- The Salesforce integration is cut from Q4 and will be revisited in the January planning; in the meantime Lena can offer a Zapier recipe as a stopgap to the two enterprise prospects.
- Offline mode for Q4 is reduced to a read-only offline job list; full offline editing is pushed to Q1.
- Deino will use a hosted status page rather than building one; Priya sets it up out of the SOC 2 budget.
- There will be a production change freeze from 18 December to 4 January, with only emergency fixes deployed.
- Aisha will propose two engineering hires to the board on 29 September: a senior backend engineer and a mobile engineer.

#### Key facts

- **What was Deino's ARR at the end of Q3 2026?** $2.4 million, up from $1.9 million at the end of Q2 (the $2.6M figure was the missed stretch target)
- **How many paying customers did Deino have at the end of Q3?** 41
- **How much engineering capacity is available in Q4?** About 30 engineer-weeks, after on-call, support, holidays, interviewing and a 4-week buffer
- **How many engineer-weeks did all seven candidate bets add up to?** 56 engineer-weeks, against 30 available
- **How big is Calendar Sync v2 estimated to be?** About 11 engineer-weeks (10 to 12)
- **Why did Lena argue for the Salesforce integration?** Two enterprise deals in the pipeline (a Midwest HVAC group and a facilities management company, about 230 technicians, roughly $165k ARR) explicitly require it
- **What is the top technician complaint about the mobile app?** The app not working without signal, 38% of technician feedback
- **Why did Priya say SOC 2 had to be a Q4 priority?** Type II is a gate for large deals like Brightkite and needs an observation window that cannot be sped up, so every month of delay pushes big deals back
- **Which customer was hit hardest by the Calendar Sync v1.4 bug and how badly?** Fernhollow, with about 130 duplicate jobs over roughly two weeks
- **How much smaller is the read-only offline job list than full offline mode?** About 4 engineer-weeks versus about 10 for full offline
- **How long does it currently take a new customer to go live?** 19 days median from contract signed to first job dispatched
- **What do the two proposed engineering hires cost?** About $420k a year fully loaded, roughly $35k a month of burn, taking runway from about 19 to a bit over 17 months

